{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- assign ratio = section.settings.image_ratio | default: 'square' -%}
<div class="non-trip non-trip--ratio-{{ ratio }}"{% if section.settings.max_height > 0 %} style="--non-trip-max: {{ section.settings.max_height }}px"{% endif %}>
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- assign alt_text = block.settings.image_alt | default: block.settings.title -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      The tile's accessible name. The caption is aria-hidden once the tile is a
      control, so this is the ONLY thing a screen reader gets — it has to carry
      what the caption was showing, not just the action. Falls back to the
      overlay copy so a merchant who writes nothing still gets a usable name
      rather than "button".
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture tile_name -%}
      {%- if block.settings.tile_label != blank -%}
        {{ block.settings.tile_label }}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ block.settings.title }}{% if block.settings.subtitle != blank %} — {{ block.settings.subtitle }}{% endif %}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign tile_name = tile_name | strip -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      THE WHOLE TILE IS THE CONTROL.

      At 280–340px tall and a third of a phone wide, a tile has no room for a
      button inside it that is also a 44px target — and a button inside a
      picture that is itself tappable is two overlapping targets with different
      outcomes. So the tile is one control, filling its own cell, and the
      caption sits on top of it rather than beside it.

      Which control it is depends on what the block is for:

        - a meal category opens the Somm with that category already supplied,
          so "mains" does not have to be typed by someone who has just tapped
          the word MAINS
        - a plain link stays a link
        - neither leaves the tile as inert editorial, which is what it was

      The accessible name is written for the action, not read off the picture:
      "Find a NON for mains" says what happens. The alt text describes the food
      and does not repeat the overlay, so a screen reader is not given the same
      three words twice.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      FOCAL POINT, PER TILE.

      Three photographs cropped to a 28/44/28 strip on a phone are three
      different crops, and `object-position: center` is only right by accident.
      A plated main shot from above wants its centre; a bottle standing in a
      frame wants its top. One shared default put the food out of frame on two
      of the three tiles at 375px.

      A custom property rather than a class per position, because the value is
      an arbitrary pair of percentages and enumerating them in CSS would cap
      what a merchant can choose at whatever list someone thought of.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      class="non-trip__cell"
      {% if block.settings.focal != blank %}style="--non-trip-pos: {{ block.settings.focal }}"{% endif %}
      {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      {%- if settings.somm_enabled and block.settings.meal_category != blank -%}
        <button
          type="button"
          class="non-trip__hit"
          data-non-somm-open
          data-somm-surface="homepage_triptych"
          data-somm-context="home"
          data-somm-meal="{{ block.settings.meal_category | escape }}"
          data-somm-position="{{ forloop.index0 }}"
          data-somm-opener="{{ block.settings.somm_question | escape }}"
          data-somm-options="{{ block.settings.somm_options | escape }}">
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ tile_name }}</span>
        </button>
      {%- elsif block.settings.link != blank -%}
        <a class="non-trip__hit" href="{{ block.settings.link }}">
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ tile_name }}</span>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if block.settings.image != blank -%}
        {{
          block.settings.image
          | image_url: width: 900, format: 'webp'
          | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '400,600,900', class: 'non-trip__img', alt: alt_text
        }}
      {%- elsif block.settings.image_url != blank -%}
        {% render 'cdn-image',
           url: block.settings.image_url,
           alt: alt_text,
           class: 'non-trip__img',
           sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 33vw, 100vw' %}
      {%- else -%}
        {{ 'lifestyle-1' | placeholder_svg_tag }}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The caption sits UNDER the tile control in the stacking order and is
        not itself clickable. It used to wrap the title in its own anchor,
        which — now that the whole tile is a control — would be a second
        target inside the first, reachable by tab, announcing the same
        destination. One control per tile.

        The anchor is only kept when there is no tile control at all, which is
        the case for a block with neither a meal category nor a link: nothing
        to click, nothing to nest.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        NOT aria-hidden.

        The first version hid the caption from assistive technology whenever
        the tile was a control, on the reasoning that the control's own name
        already carries the words. That reasoning only holds on a phone: above
        the breakpoint the tile control is display:none, so hiding the caption
        too would have removed "MAINS — charred lamb, mushroom" from a desktop
        screen reader entirely. Copy that is on the page for a sighted visitor
        and absent for a blind one is a regression, and a silent one.

        A markup-level attribute cannot know the viewport, so it does not try.
        Both are exposed: the control announces the action, the caption
        describes the tile. Mildly redundant on a phone, complete everywhere.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="non-trip__cap">
        <div class="non-trip__title">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
        <div class="non-trip__sub">{{ block.settings.subtitle }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Editorial triptych",
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_ratio",
      "label": "Image shape",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "square",
          "label": "Square (1:1)"
        },
        {
          "value": "tall",
          "label": "Tall (4:5)"
        },
        {
          "value": "portrait",
          "label": "Portrait (3:4)"
        },
        {
          "value": "landscape",
          "label": "Landscape (3:2)"
        }
      ],
      "default": "square"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_height",
      "label": "Maximum image height",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 900,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "Caps how tall the pictures may grow on a wide screen. 0 leaves them sized by the shape above."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "cell",
      "name": "Panel",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "image_picker",
          "id": "image",
          "label": "Image",
          "info": "Overrides the image URL below."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "image_url",
          "label": "Image URL",
          "info": "Used when no image is picked. Points at an image already on the store's CDN."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "image_alt",
          "label": "Image alt text",
          "info": "Describes the photo for screen readers. Falls back to the title."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title",
          "default": "Made for starters"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "subtitle",
          "label": "Subtitle",
          "default": "oysters, radicchio, cured fish"
        },
        {
          "type": "url",
          "id": "link",
          "label": "Link"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "focal",
          "label": "Focal point",
          "info": "Which part of the photo to keep when it is cropped, as two percentages: 50% 50% is the centre, 50% 30% keeps the upper third. Matters most on a phone, where the tile is narrow."
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "content": "Open the Somm instead"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "meal_category",
          "label": "Meal category",
          "info": "Fill this in — starters, mains, dessert — and tapping the tile opens the NON Somm with that already supplied instead of following the link. Leave empty to keep it a plain link."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "somm_question",
          "label": "Opening question",
          "info": "The one short question the Somm asks first, e.g. What's the main event? A category on its own is too broad to recommend from."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "somm_options",
          "label": "Answers",
          "info": "Separated by a vertical bar: Roast chicken | Lamb | Mushroom | Something spicy. Shown as chips under the question."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tile_label",
          "label": "Accessible name",
          "info": "What a screen reader announces for the whole tile, e.g. Find a NON for mains. Falls back to the title and subtitle."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Editorial triptych"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

